3) The disciplinary committee of a State Bar Council after giving the advocate concerned and the Advocate-General an opportunity of being heard, may make any of the following orders, namely:
Sri. Paras Jain vs Karnataka State Bar Council on 7 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/100590463/
4 a) dismiss the complaint or, where the proceedings were initiated at the instance of the State Bar Council, direct that the proceedings be filed;
 (b) reprimand the advocate;
 (c) suspend the advocate from practice for such period  as it may deem fit;
 (d) remove the name of the advocate from the State roll  of advocates.
